---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import { giving } from '@/config/site';

/**
 * The Tragedy. Chapter one of Road to Her Smile.
 *
 * Copy is the verbatim record of the live campaign page in
 * reference/MIGRATION.md, section 2.2, set in the house style. The old site
 * misspelled this page. It is "Tragedy" everywhere here: route, title, h1, links.
 */
const card = giving.find((method) => method.id === 'card');
const cardHref = card?.detail.value ?? '';

/** Carried across from the existing campaign page, where they appear verbatim. */
const inheritedStats = [
  { value: '13', label: 'Teeth removed in a single procedure' },
  { value: '0', label: 'Follow-up calls received afterward' },
  { value: '$25', label: 'What she was given when she asked for help' },
];
---

<Base
  title="The Tragedy"
  description="What happened to Lia Spriggs. The full story of medical abandonment, institutional betrayal, and the road to restoration."
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="section hero">
    <div class="wrap hero__grid">
      <div class="hero__copy">
        <span class="label">Road to Her Smile. Chapter one</span>
        <h1>The <span class="em">Tragedy</span></h1>
        <p class="hero__sub">What was done to Lia Spriggs. Thirteen teeth. One doctor. No answers.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero__media">
        <div class="ph-frame" style="--ph-ratio: 4 / 5">
          Lia, Verona<br />photograph to follow
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Before -->
  <section class="section section--white">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <span class="label">Before</span>
      <h2>She was not always <span class="em">invisible</span></h2>
      <p>
        Lia Spriggs was born in Verona, Italy, into a life that carried the kind of natural,
        unhurried elegance that luxury brands spend millions trying to manufacture, and she moved
        through the fashion world of northern Italy as someone whose presence alone could hold a
        room still, a woman with a future that looked genuinely expansive and entirely her own.
      </p>
      <p>
        On a military post in Vicenza, she met a man in uniform who promised her love, a life in
        America, and the kind of partnership she had every reason to believe was real, and she
        left behind everything she had ever known to follow him across the ocean into what she
        trusted would be a shared future.
      </p>
      <p>
        Over the course of twelve years of marriage, Lia discovered that her husband had been
        unfaithful for nearly all of them, a sustained betrayal that left her isolated as a single
        immigrant mother raising two children in a country that was not her own, with no family
        within reach and no safety net of any kind beneath her.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Betrayal -->
  <section class="section section--sand">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <span class="label">The betrayal</span>
      <h2>Thirteen teeth. One doctor. <span class="em">No</span> answers.</h2>
      <p>
        When an eviction notice brought Lia to her knees in front of her children, she found a
        trusted community that offered what felt like solid ground, and through that community
        she was referred to a doctor who she believed would restore what years of hardship had
        already begun to erode.
      </p>
      <p>
        That doctor extracted thirteen of her teeth in a single procedure, and then he vanished
        without explanation, leaving behind no implants, no replacement teeth, no follow-up
        appointment, and no way for Lia to reach him, abandoning her toothless and without
        recourse in a situation she had no power to reverse on her own.
      </p>
      <p>
        When Lia returned to that same community and asked for help, they gave her a twenty-five
        dollar grocery gift card, and just days later, from that same organization, came the
        announcement of a seven point two million dollar renovation project, a contrast so
        enormous and so quiet that it became the central image this documentary exists to hold
        up to the light.
      </p>

      <blockquote class="pull">
        <p>She was not asking for luxury. She was asking for her dignity.</p>
      </blockquote>

      <div class="ph-frame ph-frame--wide" style="--ph-ratio: 16 / 9">
        The chair. No follow-up. No answers.<br />image to follow
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Medical Reality -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <span class="label">The medical reality</span>
      <h2>This is not a production choice. This is a <span class="em">medical</span> fact.</h2>
      <p>
        In the years following the extraction, Lia's body developed both Hashimoto's disease and
        fibromyalgia, and she now lives every day with an ill-fitting denture that causes constant
        pain, while the bone loss in her jaw continues to progress at a rate that means the window
        for surgical intervention is actively closing with each month that passes.
      </p>
      <p>
        Without intervention, the bone deterioration will advance to the point where dental
        implants are no longer a viable option at all, and what is at stake is not a cosmetic
        concern but a woman's fundamental ability to eat solid food, to speak clearly without
        discomfort, and to smile without the sharp, grinding pain that has defined her daily
        reality for nearly two decades.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Inherited stat block -->
  <section class="section section--white">
    <div class="wrap">
      <ul class="stats">
        {
          inheritedStats.map((stat) => (
            <li class="stats__item">
              <span class="stats__value">{stat.value}</span>
              <span class="stats__label">{stat.label}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <p class="stats__note">Figures as stated on the existing Road to Her Smile campaign page.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTAs and chapter navigation -->
  <section class="section section--sand">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <span class="label">Her road back</span>
      <h2>Support Lia's <span class="em">restoration</span></h2>
      <p>
        Every contribution funds production, legal advocacy, and Lia's medical restoration. This
        is how we make sure her voice is finally heard.
      </p>
      <div class="ctas">
        {
          cardHref ? (
            <a href={cardHref} class="btn btn--primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              Support Lia's Restoration
            </a>
          ) : (
            <span class="btn btn--primary" aria-disabled="true">
              Support Lia's Restoration
            </span>
          )
        }
        <a href="/road-to-her-smile/her-road" class="btn btn--ghost">Read Her Full Road</a>
      </div>

      <hr class="rule" />

      <nav class="chapter-nav" aria-label="Road to Her Smile chapters">
        <a class="chapter-nav__link" href="/road-to-her-smile">
          <span class="chapter-nav__kicker">Back</span>
          <span class="chapter-nav__title">Road to Her Smile</span>
        </a>
        <a class="chapter-nav__link chapter-nav__link--next" href="/road-to-her-smile/her-road">
          <span class="chapter-nav__kicker">Next chapter</span>
          <span class="chapter-nav__title">Her Road <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></span>
        </a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-xl);
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media (min-width: 52rem) {
    .hero__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 0.85fr;
      gap: var(--space-2xl);
    }
  }

  .hero__sub {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.3;
    max-width: 32ch;
  }

  .hero__media .ph-frame {
    width: 100%;
  }

  .pull {
    margin: var(--space-xl) 0;
    padding-left: var(--space-m);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--gold);
  }

  .pull p {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .ph-frame--wide {
    width: 100%;
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .stats {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: var(--space-xl) 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-l);
    text-align: center;
    border-block: 1px solid var(--gold);
  }

  @media (min-width: 40rem) {
    .stats {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }

    .stats__item + .stats__item {
      border-left: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--gold) 50%, transparent);
    }
  }

  .stats__value {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-4);
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--teal-ink);
  }

  .stats__label {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--2);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--track-widest);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: var(--space-xs) auto 0;
    max-width: 22ch;
  }

  .stats__note {
    text-align: center;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: var(--space-m) auto 0;
  }

  .ctas {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-2xs);
  }

  .chapter-nav {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-m);
  }

  .chapter-nav__link {
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .chapter-nav__link--next {
    text-align: right;
    margin-left: auto;
  }

  .chapter-nav__kicker {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--2);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--track-widest);
    color: var(--gold-ink);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3xs);
  }

  .chapter-nav__title {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
    transition: border-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease);
  }

  .chapter-nav__link:hover .chapter-nav__title {
    border-bottom-color: var(--gold);
  }
</style>
